<BlogArticle
	title="How to Apply for a Minor’s PAN Card"
	description="Learn how a parent or guardian applies for a minor’s PAN card, which current Indian form to choose, and what documents may be required."
	canonicalUrl="https://nsdlphotoresize.com/blogs/minor-pan-card/"
	heading="How to apply for a minor’s PAN card"
	intro="A child’s PAN application is made with an adult acting as the representative assessee. Use the current application instructions and the child’s own supporting details; do not apply for a second PAN if one has already been allotted."
>
	<section class="space-y-3">
		<h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">Choose the current form and route</h2>
		<p>
			For an Indian individual, Protean’s current guidance uses Form
			93 for a new PAN application; UTIITSL directs Indian new
			applicants to Forms 93/94. Form 93’s instructions state that a
			representative assessee is mandatory when the applicant is a
			minor. The parent or legal guardian should complete that section
			as the application directs.
		</p>
		<p>
			Do not use the old Form 49A process based on older articles:
			official provider pages state the new forms apply from
			1 April 2026. The current live application is the authority for
			which fields and verification methods are available.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="space-y-3">
		<h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">Gather the child’s and representative’s details</h2>
		<p>
			Prepare the child’s legal name, date of birth, address, and the
			identity details requested by the application. Under Protean’s
			published Form 93 document list, a minor’s Aadhaar is relevant,
			and accepted documents belonging to a parent or guardian can be
			used as the minor’s proof of identity and address. You still need
			to provide the child’s date-of-birth evidence as instructed.
		</p>
		<p>
			Protean’s Form 93 list specifically says a birth certificate
			issued by an authorised registrar/municipal authority (or
			applicable Indian Consulate) is mandatory as DOB proof for
			individuals born on or after 1 October 2023. Review the current
			list for other dates of birth and accepted evidence.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="space-y-3">
		<h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">Submit and follow the application</h2>
		<ol class="list-decimal space-y-3 pl-6">
			<li>Start at the official Protean or UTIITSL portal and select the new-PAN application for an Indian individual.</li>
			<li>Enter the child’s information and complete the representative assessee section as the form requires.</li>
			<li>Upload or submit the child’s supporting documents and any parent/guardian documents accepted for identity or address proof.</li>
			<li>Provide photo, signature, Aadhaar, consent, or verification items only as requested by the chosen live flow. Image requirements can differ by provider and submission method.</li>
			<li>Review names, dates, addresses, and document uploads before submission. Save the acknowledgement number and use the provider’s status service to track the request.</li>
		</ol>
		<p>
			Photo requirements for minors are especially form-specific.
			Older instructions may say a guardian’s photo is used in some
			circumstances; do not assume this applies to current Forms 93/94.
			Follow the exact image field instructions shown for the child’s
			application.
		</p>
	</section>

	<p>
		Read the official <a class="text-link" href="https://tinpan.proteantech.in/services/pan/documents-form_93-form_94.html">Form 93/94 document list</a>
		and <a class="text-link" href="https://tinpan.proteantech.in/services/pan/instructions-form_93-form_94.html">Form 93/94 instructions</a>,
		or visit <a class="text-link" href="https://www.pan.utiitsl.com/PAN/newA.html">UTIITSL’s current new-PAN page</a>.
	</p>
</BlogArticle>
